body:
I just tried on Windows Seven with Internet Explorer 11, and indeed the GUI is not updating. For the moment I only noticed that in this function:

``` javascript
$http.get('/rest/connections').success(function (data) {
    // Here data == $scope.connections

    var now = Date.now(),
        td = (now - prevDate) / 1000,
        id;

    prevDate = now;
    $scope.inbps = 0;
    $scope.outbps = 0;

    for (id in data) {
        if (!data.hasOwnProperty(id)) {
            continue;
        }
        try {
            data[id].inbps = Math.max(0, 8 * (data[id].InBytesTotal - $scope.connections[id].InBytesTotal) / td);
            data[id].outbps = Math.max(0, 8 * (data[id].OutBytesTotal - $scope.connections[id].OutBytesTotal) / td);
        } catch (e) {
            data[id].inbps = 0;
            data[id].outbps = 0;
        }
        $scope.inbps += data[id].inbps;
        $scope.outbps += data[id].outbps;
    }
    $scope.connections = data;
});
```

`data` is always the same as `$scope.connections`, even at the beginning of the function, which makes

``` jasvascript
data[id].inbps = Math.max(0, 8 * (data[id].InBytesTotal - $scope.connections[id].InBytesTotal) / td);
data[id].outbps = Math.max(0, 8 * (data[id].OutBytesTotal - $scope.connections[id].OutBytesTotal) / td);
```

always equal to 0.

Not sure why it is the case though.
